{"case_id":"C005","impact_scope":[{"type":"api_protocol_change","files":["std/vp8/decode_vp8.wuffs"],"functions":["decoder.set_quirk!","decoder.get_quirk","decoder.decode_image_config?","decoder.do_decode_image_config?"],"description":"The existing public VP8 decoder now requires callers to set base.QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH before decode_image_config; missing, invalid, and excessive values produce new statuses."},{"type":"configuration_change","files":["std/webp/decode_webp.wuffs"],"functions":["decoder.do_decode_image_config_limited?"],"description":"The WebP decoder adapts its existing lossy-VP8 path by deriving the VP8 source length from the WebP chunk and setting the new quirk internally."},{"type":"internal_only","files":["std/vp8/common_consts.wuffs","std/vp8/decode_bitstream.wuffs","std/vp8/decode_first_partition.wuffs","std/vp8/decode_vp8.wuffs"],"functions":["decoder.read_bit!","decoder.read_unsigned!","decoder.read_signed!","decoder.copy_partitions_to_workbuf?","decoder.decode_first_partition!","decoder.decode_other_partition_lengths!","decoder.decode_frame?","decoder.workbuf_len"],"description":"VP8 frame parsing and entropy-decoder implementation are expanded and now require a dynamically sized work buffer; H0 already obtains workbuf_len and allocates that buffer through the generic image-decoder interface."}],"gap_before":{"exists":true,"type":"existing direct VP8 public-entry exposure gap","evidence":["In S0, decoder already publicly implemented base.image_decoder and exposed decode_image_config?, but H0 instantiated only wuffs_webp__decoder and passed its WebP image-decoder upcast to fuzz_image_decoder.","S0 set_quirk! always returned #unsupported option, so direct VP8 callers had no source-length configuration action for H0 to perform.","For the WebP-mediated path, H0 already supplied arbitrary WebP bytes and exercised the standard image-decoder call sequence."]},"gap_after":{"exists":true,"type":"aggravated direct VP8 entry and configuration-protocol gap","evidence":["H0 remains limited to wuffs_webp__decoder and still never instantiates or directly calls the public VP8 decoder.","S1 decoder.do_decode_image_config? rejects a direct VP8 call with #missing QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH unless base.QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH was first configured with the required encoded length.","The WebP wrapper performs set_quirk! internally, so H0 can exercise the changed WebP-mediated VP8 path without modification; however, it cannot control or validate the new direct-VP8 caller protocol.","H0's generic helper already queries workbuf_len and dynamically allocates the returned size, so the increased VP8 work-buffer requirement is not an additional gap."]},"new_harness_obligation":{"exists":true,"description":"A harness covering the existing direct VP8 public entry must now call decoder.set_quirk! with base.QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH and a value encoding the input length before decode_image_config?. This caller-supplied configuration action did not exist in S0. The existing WebP harness needs no such action because the WebP decoder supplies it internally.","evidence":["S0 decoder.set_quirk! unconditionally returned #unsupported option.","S1 decoder.set_quirk! accepts base.QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH and stores the caller-provided value.","S1 decoder.do_decode_image_config? checks that value before parsing and returns #missing QUIRK_SOURCE_LENGTH when it was not set.","S1 WebP decoding sets the quirk from sub_chunk_length before invoking the VP8 decoder, demonstrating that the action is a concrete caller-side protocol requirement rather than merely internal VP8 state."]},"explicit_failure":false,"delta_attribution":"AGGRAVATED","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":96,"reason":"The unchanged H0 already omitted the direct public VP8 entry in S0, so a same-scope gap existed before. S1 concretely adds a mandatory caller-controlled source-length configuration step for that entry. Although H0's WebP path supplies the quirk internally and its generic work-buffer handling remains adequate, the new direct-entry protocol is an additional harness action absent in S0, making the pre-existing gap AGGRAVATED."}
